IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `lga-nouns`
IMPORT `lga-time`

-- Legislation Act 2003 (Commonwealth), Chapter 3 Part 2: parliamentary scrutiny of legislative instruments (sections 38 to 48).
-- Text: C2004A01224.txt, compilation C2019C00084; it is not the authorised text.
-- Same conventions as lga-register.l4: JUST TRUE (the text says yes), JUST FALSE (the text says no), NOTHING (the text does not say).
-- The sitting-day periods ("within 6 sitting days", "within 15 sitting days") are counted by lga-time.l4 from a calendar of sitting days given as an input;
-- the rules below take the result of that count (a yes or no) as a fact, except where a rule itself needs the day.

§ `Sections 38 and 39: tabling`

-- jural: claim of each House | duty of the Office of Parliamentary Counsel
-- src:721 | (1) The Office of Parliamentary Counsel must arrange for a copy of each registered legislative instrument to be delivered to each House of the Parliament to be laid before each House within 6 sitting days of that House after the registration of the instrument.
@ref s 38(1) (src:721-721)
GIVEN `it is a registered legislative instrument` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 38(1): the Office of Parliamentary Counsel must arrange for a copy to be delivered to each House to be laid within 6 sitting days of that House after registration` MEANS
    IF `it is a registered legislative instrument` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- Section 38(3) says "the last day for it to be so laid" and each House has its own last day: the later of the two is taken (fork), and the repeal is immediately after the end of that day, so the first day without the instrument is the next day.
-- src:722 | (3) If a copy of a legislative instrument is not laid before each House of the Parliament in accordance with this section, the legislative instrument is repealed immediately after the last day for it to be so laid.
@ref s 38(3) (src:722-722)
GIVEN `a copy of the legislative instrument is not laid before each House in accordance with section 38` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 38(3): the legislative instrument is repealed` MEANS
    IF `a copy of the legislative instrument is not laid before each House in accordance with section 38` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE

@ref s 38(3) (src:722-722)
GIVEN `the last day for it to be laid before the House of Representatives` IS A DATE
      `the last day for it to be laid before the Senate` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 38(3): the first day on which the legislative instrument is no longer in force for not being laid` MEANS
    (`the later of two days` `the last day for it to be laid before the House of Representatives` `the last day for it to be laid before the Senate`) PLUS 1

-- jural: claim of each House | duty of the Office of Parliamentary Counsel
-- src:724 | (1) If an explanatory statement for a legislative instrument is registered, the Office of Parliamentary Counsel must arrange for a copy of the explanatory statement to be delivered to each House of the Parliament, to be laid before each House.
@ref s 39(1) (src:724-724)
GIVEN `an explanatory statement for a legislative instrument is registered` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 39(1): the Office of Parliamentary Counsel must arrange for a copy of the explanatory statement to be delivered to each House to be laid` MEANS
    IF `an explanatory statement for a legislative instrument is registered` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

DECLARE `Kind of explanatory statement for section 39` IS ONE OF
    `an initial explanatory statement to be delivered under section 39`
    `a supplementary explanatory statement or replacement explanatory statement`

-- jural: claim of each House | duty of the Office of Parliamentary Counsel
-- Paragraph (a)(i): for an initial statement, at the same time as the instrument if practicable; otherwise (ii).
-- src:725 | (2) The delivery to each House of the Parliament must be arranged:
-- src:726 | (a) in the case of an initial explanatory statement:
-- src:727 | (i) if practicable, at the same time as a copy of the instrument is delivered to that House under section 38; or
-- src:728 | (ii) in any other case—within 6 sitting days of that House after registration of the explanatory statement; or
-- src:729 | (b) in the case of a supplementary explanatory statement or replacement explanatory statement—within 6 sitting days of that House after registration of the explanatory statement.
@ref s 39(2) (src:725-729)
GIVEN `the kind` IS A `Kind of explanatory statement for section 39`
      `it is practicable to deliver it at the same time as a copy of the instrument is delivered under section 38` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 39(2)(a)(i): the delivery must be arranged at the same time as the instrument is delivered under section 38` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the kind`
    WHEN `an initial explanatory statement to be delivered under section 39` THEN (IF `it is practicable to deliver it at the same time as a copy of the instrument is delivered under section 38` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE)
    WHEN `a supplementary explanatory statement or replacement explanatory statement` THEN NOTHING

-- The last day of the 6 sitting days after the day the explanatory statement is registered (paragraphs (a)(ii) and (b)).
@ref s 39(2)(a)(ii) and (b) (src:727-729)
GIVEN `the sitting days of the House, in date order` IS A LIST OF DATE
      `the day the explanatory statement was registered` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 39(2)(a)(ii) and (b): the last day for delivering the explanatory statement to the House` MEANS
    `the nth sitting day after a day` 6 `the sitting days of the House, in date order` `the day the explanatory statement was registered`

-- jural: claim of the House | duty of the rule-maker
-- src:730 | (3) If the initial explanatory statement for a legislative instrument is lodged by the rule-maker for registration too late for it to be delivered to a House of the Parliament at the same time as a copy of the instrument, the rule-maker must, as soon as possible, deliver to that House a written statement explaining the lateness of lodgement.
@ref s 39(3) (src:730-730)
GIVEN `the initial explanatory statement is lodged by the rule-maker for registration too late for it to be delivered to the House at the same time as a copy of the instrument` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 39(3): the rule-maker must, as soon as possible, deliver to the House a written statement explaining the lateness of lodgement` MEANS
    IF `the initial explanatory statement is lodged by the rule-maker for registration too late for it to be delivered to the House at the same time as a copy of the instrument` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:731 | (4) If a replacement explanatory statement replacing an initial explanatory statement is registered before the initial explanatory statement is delivered to each House of the Parliament under subsection (1):
-- src:732 | (a) this section stops applying to the initial explanatory statement; and
-- src:733 | (b) this section applies to the replacement explanatory statement as if it were the initial explanatory statement.
-- src:734 | Note: For initial explanatory statements and supplementary and replacement explanatory statements, see section 15J.
@ref s 39(4) (src:731-734)
GIVEN `a replacement explanatory statement replacing an initial explanatory statement is registered before the initial explanatory statement is delivered to each House under subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 39(4): this section stops applying to the initial explanatory statement and applies to the replacement as if it were the initial explanatory statement` MEANS
    IF `a replacement explanatory statement replacing an initial explanatory statement is registered before the initial explanatory statement is delivered to each House under subsection (1)` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE

§ `Section 41: incorporated material`

-- jural: power of a House | liability of the rule-maker or the Office of Parliamentary Counsel
-- "at any time while a legislative instrument is subject to disallowance": outside that time the answer is JUST FALSE.
-- src:738 | A House of the Parliament may, at any time while a legislative instrument is subject to disallowance, require any document incorporated by reference in the instrument to be made available for inspection by that House:
-- src:739 | (a) at a place acceptable to the House; and
-- src:740 | (b) at a time specified by the House.
@ref s 41 (src:738-740)
GIVEN `the legislative instrument is subject to disallowance` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the document is incorporated by reference in the instrument` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 41: the House may require the document to be made available for inspection` MEANS
    IF NOT `the legislative instrument is subject to disallowance` THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE (IF `the document is incorporated by reference in the instrument` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING)

§ `Section 42: disallowance`

-- Paragraph (a) and (b) are tested by the calendar in lga-time.l4; here they are facts: notice given within 15 sitting days; resolution passed within 15 sitting days after the notice.
-- jural: power of a House | liability of the legislative instrument and the person relying on it
-- src:742 | (1) If:
-- src:743 | (a) notice of a motion to disallow a legislative instrument or a provision of a legislative instrument is given in a House of the Parliament within 15 sitting days of that House beginning on the first sitting day after a copy of the instrument was laid before that House; and
-- src:744 | (b) within 15 sitting days of that House beginning on the first sitting day after the giving of that notice, the House passes a resolution, in pursuance of the motion, disallowing the instrument or provision;
-- src:745 | the instrument or provision so disallowed is repealed immediately after the passing of that resolution.
@ref s 42(1) (src:742-745)
GIVEN `notice of a motion to disallow the instrument or a provision is given in a House within 15 sitting days of that House beginning on the first sitting day after a copy of the instrument was laid before that House` IS A BOOLEAN
      `within 15 sitting days of that House beginning on the first sitting day after the giving of that notice, the House passes a resolution, in pursuance of the motion, disallowing the instrument or provision` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 42(1): the instrument or provision so disallowed is repealed immediately after the passing of that resolution` MEANS
    IF `notice of a motion to disallow the instrument or a provision is given in a House within 15 sitting days of that House beginning on the first sitting day after a copy of the instrument was laid before that House`
       AND `within 15 sitting days of that House beginning on the first sitting day after the giving of that notice, the House passes a resolution, in pursuance of the motion, disallowing the instrument or provision`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- src:746 | (2) If:
-- src:747 | (a) notice of a motion to disallow a legislative instrument or a provision of a legislative instrument is given in a House of the Parliament within 15 sitting days of that House beginning on the first sitting day after a copy of the instrument was laid before that House; and
-- src:748 | (b) at the end of 15 sitting days of that House beginning on the first sitting day after the giving of that notice of motion:
-- src:749 | (i) the notice has not been withdrawn and the motion has not been called on; or
-- src:750 | (ii) the motion has been called on, moved and (where relevant) seconded and has not been withdrawn or otherwise disposed of;
-- src:751 | the instrument or provision specified in the motion is then taken to have been disallowed and is repealed at that time.
@ref s 42(2) (src:746-751)
GIVEN `notice of a motion to disallow the instrument or a provision is given in a House within 15 sitting days of that House beginning on the first sitting day after a copy of the instrument was laid before that House` IS A BOOLEAN
      `at the end of 15 sitting days of that House beginning on the first sitting day after the giving of that notice, the notice has not been withdrawn and the motion has not been called on` IS A BOOLEAN
      `at the end of those 15 sitting days, the motion has been called on, moved and (where relevant) seconded and has not been withdrawn or otherwise disposed of` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 42(2): the instrument or provision is taken to have been disallowed and is repealed at that time` MEANS
    IF `notice of a motion to disallow the instrument or a provision is given in a House within 15 sitting days of that House beginning on the first sitting day after a copy of the instrument was laid before that House`
       AND (`at the end of 15 sitting days of that House beginning on the first sitting day after the giving of that notice, the notice has not been withdrawn and the motion has not been called on`
            OR `at the end of those 15 sitting days, the motion has been called on, moved and (where relevant) seconded and has not been withdrawn or otherwise disposed of`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- src:752 | (3) If:
-- src:753 | (a) notice of a motion to disallow a legislative instrument or a provision of a legislative instrument is given in a House of the Parliament within 15 sitting days of that House beginning on the first sitting day after a copy of the instrument was laid before that House; and
-- src:754 | (b) before the end of 15 sitting days of that House beginning on the first sitting day after the giving of that notice of motion, the House of Representatives is dissolved or expires, or the Parliament is prorogued; and
-- src:755 | (c) at the time of the dissolution, expiry or prorogation, as the case may be:
-- src:756 | (i) the notice has not been withdrawn and the motion has not been called on; or
-- src:757 | (ii) the motion has been called on, moved and (where relevant) seconded and has not been withdrawn or otherwise disposed of;
-- src:758 | the legislative instrument is taken, for the purposes of subsections (1) and (2), to have been laid before the first-mentioned House on the first sitting day of that first-mentioned House after the dissolution, expiry or prorogation, as the case may be.
@ref s 42(3) (src:752-758)
GIVEN `notice of a motion to disallow the instrument or a provision is given in a House within 15 sitting days of that House beginning on the first sitting day after a copy of the instrument was laid before that House` IS A BOOLEAN
      `before the end of 15 sitting days beginning on the first sitting day after the giving of that notice, the House of Representatives is dissolved or expires, or the Parliament is prorogued` IS A BOOLEAN
      `at the time of the dissolution, expiry or prorogation the notice has not been withdrawn and the motion has not been called on` IS A BOOLEAN
      `at the time of the dissolution, expiry or prorogation the motion has been called on, moved and (where relevant) seconded and has not been withdrawn or otherwise disposed of` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 42(3): the instrument is taken to have been laid before the House on the first sitting day of that House after the dissolution, expiry or prorogation` MEANS
    IF `notice of a motion to disallow the instrument or a provision is given in a House within 15 sitting days of that House beginning on the first sitting day after a copy of the instrument was laid before that House`
       AND `before the end of 15 sitting days beginning on the first sitting day after the giving of that notice, the House of Representatives is dissolved or expires, or the Parliament is prorogued`
       AND (`at the time of the dissolution, expiry or prorogation the notice has not been withdrawn and the motion has not been called on`
            OR `at the time of the dissolution, expiry or prorogation the motion has been called on, moved and (where relevant) seconded and has not been withdrawn or otherwise disposed of`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE

@ref s 42(3) (src:758-758)
GIVEN `the sitting days of the House, in date order` IS A LIST OF DATE
      `the day of the dissolution, expiry or prorogation` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 42(3): the day the instrument is taken to have been laid` MEANS
    `the first sitting day after a day` `the sitting days of the House, in date order` `the day of the dissolution, expiry or prorogation`

§ `Section 44: instruments not subject to disallowance`

-- "unless the instrument is a regulation, or the enabling legislation or some other Act has the effect that the instrument is disallowable".
-- src:760 | (1) Section 42 does not apply in relation to a legislative instrument, or a provision of a legislative instrument if the enabling legislation for the instrument (not being the Corporations Act 2001):
-- src:761 | (a) facilitates the establishment or operation of an intergovernmental body or scheme involving the Commonwealth and one or more States or Territories; and
-- src:762 | (b) authorises the instrument to be made by the body or for the purposes of the body or scheme;
-- src:763 | unless the instrument is a regulation, or the enabling legislation or some other Act has the effect that the instrument is disallowable.
@ref s 44(1) (src:760-763)
GIVEN `the enabling legislation (not being the Corporations Act 2001) facilitates the establishment or operation of an intergovernmental body or scheme involving the Commonwealth and one or more States or Territories` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the enabling legislation authorises the instrument to be made by the body or for the purposes of the body or scheme` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the instrument is a regulation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the enabling legislation or some other Act has the effect that the instrument is disallowable` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 44(1): section 42 does not apply in relation to the instrument` MEANS
    IF `the enabling legislation (not being the Corporations Act 2001) facilitates the establishment or operation of an intergovernmental body or scheme involving the Commonwealth and one or more States or Territories`
       AND `the enabling legislation authorises the instrument to be made by the body or for the purposes of the body or scheme`
       AND NOT `the instrument is a regulation`
       AND NOT `the enabling legislation or some other Act has the effect that the instrument is disallowable`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- src:764 | (2) Section 42 does not apply in relation to a legislative instrument, or a provision of a legislative instrument, if:
-- src:765 | (a) an Act declares, or has the effect, that section 42 does not apply in relation to the instrument or provision; or
-- src:766 | (b) the legislative instrument is prescribed by regulation for the purposes of this paragraph.
@ref s 44(2) (src:764-766)
GIVEN `an Act declares, or has the effect, that section 42 does not apply in relation to the instrument or provision` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the legislative instrument is prescribed by regulation for the purposes of paragraph 44(2)(b)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 44(2): section 42 does not apply in relation to the instrument or provision` MEANS
    IF `an Act declares, or has the effect, that section 42 does not apply in relation to the instrument or provision` OR `the legislative instrument is prescribed by regulation for the purposes of paragraph 44(2)(b)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- src:767 | (3) Prescribing a kind of instrument by regulation for the purposes of paragraph (2)(b) does not imply that every instrument of that kind is a legislative instrument.
@ref s 44(3) (src:767-767)
GIVEN `a kind of instrument is prescribed by regulation for the purposes of paragraph (2)(b)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 44(3): prescribing the kind implies that every instrument of that kind is a legislative instrument` MEANS
    IF `a kind of instrument is prescribed by regulation for the purposes of paragraph (2)(b)` THEN JUST FALSE ELSE NOTHING

-- Section 42 applies to a legislative instrument unless section 44 or subsection 51(4) says it does not (section 4: "disallowable legislative instrument").
-- src:85 | disallowable legislative instrument means a legislative instrument to which section 42 applies.
-- src:86 | Note: Section 42 provides for the parliamentary disallowance of legislative instruments. Section 42 does not apply to some legislative instruments (see section 44).
@ref s 4 "disallowable legislative instrument" (src:85-86)
GIVEN `section 42 does not apply because of subsection 44(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `section 42 does not apply because of subsection 44(2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `section 42 does not apply because of subsection 51(4)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 4: the legislative instrument is a disallowable legislative instrument` MEANS
    IF `section 42 does not apply because of subsection 44(1)` OR `section 42 does not apply because of subsection 44(2)` OR `section 42 does not apply because of subsection 51(4)`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE JUST TRUE

§ `Section 45: reviving a legislative instrument, law or provision`

-- src:769 | (2) If:
-- src:770 | (a) a legislative instrument (the repealing instrument) or a provision (the repealing provision) of a legislative instrument is repealed by subsection 38(3) or 42(1) or (2) at a particular time (the repeal time); and
-- src:771 | (b) the repealing instrument or repealing provision wholly or partly repealed another legislative instrument or law, or a provision of another legislative instrument or law, that was in force immediately before the repealing instrument or repealing provision commenced;
-- src:772 | the instrument, law or provision repealed by the repealing instrument or repealing provision revives from the repeal time as if the repealing instrument or repealing provision had not been made.
-- src:773 | (3) Subsection (2) does not have the effect of reviving a legislative instrument, law or provision if, before the date when it would have been revived, Part 4 (sunsetting of legislative instruments) would have repealed it had it not already been repealed by the repealing instrument or the repealing provision.
@ref s 45(2) and (3) (src:769-773)
GIVEN `the repealing instrument or provision is repealed by subsection 38(3) or 42(1) or (2) at a particular time` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the repealing instrument or provision wholly or partly repealed another legislative instrument or law, or a provision of one, that was in force immediately before the repealing instrument or provision commenced` IS A BOOLEAN
      `Part 4 would have repealed the repealed instrument, law or provision before the date when it would have been revived, had it not already been repealed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 45: the instrument, law or provision repealed by the repealing instrument or provision revives from the repeal time` MEANS
    IF `Part 4 would have repealed the repealed instrument, law or provision before the date when it would have been revived, had it not already been repealed` THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE
        IF `the repealing instrument or provision is repealed by subsection 38(3) or 42(1) or (2) at a particular time`
           AND `the repealing instrument or provision wholly or partly repealed another legislative instrument or law, or a provision of one, that was in force immediately before the repealing instrument or provision commenced`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE

§ `Sections 46 to 48: not remaking an instrument`

-- Section 46(1): the period is fixed in the text's own words (46(2), counted in lga-time.l4), so a day outside it answers JUST FALSE.
-- "unless both Houses of the Parliament by resolution approve": approval answers JUST FALSE.
-- jural: immunity of the Parliament's scrutiny of the original instrument | disability of the rule-maker to remake it
-- src:775 | (1) If a legislative instrument (the original legislative instrument) has been registered, no legislative instrument the same in substance as the original legislative instrument is to be made during the period defined by subsection (2) unless both Houses of the Parliament by resolution approve the making of an instrument the same in substance as the original legislative instrument.
@ref s 46(1) (src:775-775)
GIVEN `the original legislative instrument has been registered` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the new instrument is the same in substance as the original legislative instrument` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the new instrument would be made falls in the period defined by subsection (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `both Houses of the Parliament by resolution approve the making of an instrument the same in substance as the original` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 46(1): the same legislative instrument is not to be made during the period` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the original legislative instrument has been registered` AND `the new instrument is the same in substance as the original legislative instrument`) THEN NOTHING
    ELSE
        IF NOT `the day the new instrument would be made falls in the period defined by subsection (2)` THEN JUST FALSE
        ELSE (IF `both Houses of the Parliament by resolution approve the making of an instrument the same in substance as the original` THEN JUST FALSE ELSE JUST TRUE)

-- The period of subsection (2) runs to the end of 7 days after the later of the Houses' last days where the instrument has not been laid before both (fork); lga-time.l4 counts it.
-- src:780 | (3) An instrument made in contravention of this section has no effect.
@ref s 46(3) (src:780-780)
GIVEN `the instrument is made in contravention of section 46` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 46(3): the instrument made in contravention has effect` MEANS
    IF `the instrument is made in contravention of section 46` THEN JUST FALSE ELSE NOTHING

-- jural: immunity of the Parliament's scrutiny of the original instrument | disability of the rule-maker to remake it
-- Section 47(1): the prohibition applies where notice was given in time and none of the four releases has happened ("must not be made unless").
-- src:782 | (1) If notice of a motion to disallow a legislative instrument, or a provision of a legislative instrument, has been given in a House of the Parliament within 15 sitting days of that House beginning on the first sitting day after the instrument was laid before that House, a legislative instrument, or a provision of a legislative instrument, that is the same in substance as the first-mentioned instrument or provision, must not be made unless:
-- src:783 | (a) the notice has been withdrawn; or
-- src:784 | (b) the instrument or provision is taken to have been disallowed under subsection 42(2); or
-- src:785 | (c) the motion has been withdrawn or otherwise disposed of; or
-- src:786 | (d) subsection 42(3) has applied in relation to the instrument.
@ref s 47(1) (src:782-786)
GIVEN `notice of a motion to disallow the instrument or a provision has been given in a House within 15 sitting days of that House beginning on the first sitting day after the instrument was laid before that House` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice has been withdrawn` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the instrument or provision is taken to have been disallowed under subsection 42(2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the motion has been withdrawn or otherwise disposed of` IS A BOOLEAN
      `subsection 42(3) has applied in relation to the instrument` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 47(1): the same legislative instrument or provision must not be made` MEANS
    IF NOT `notice of a motion to disallow the instrument or a provision has been given in a House within 15 sitting days of that House beginning on the first sitting day after the instrument was laid before that House` THEN NOTHING
    ELSE
        IF `the notice has been withdrawn` OR `the instrument or provision is taken to have been disallowed under subsection 42(2)` OR `the motion has been withdrawn or otherwise disposed of` OR `subsection 42(3) has applied in relation to the instrument`
        THEN JUST FALSE
        ELSE JUST TRUE

-- jural: immunity of the Parliament's scrutiny of the original instrument | disability of the rule-maker to remake it
-- src:787 | (2) If:
-- src:788 | (a) because of subsection 42(3), a legislative instrument is taken to have been laid before a House of the Parliament on a particular day; and
-- src:789 | (b) notice of a motion to disallow the instrument or a provision of the instrument has been given in that House within 15 sitting days of that House beginning on the first sitting day after that day;
-- src:790 | a legislative instrument, or a provision of a legislative instrument, that is the same in substance as the first-mentioned instrument or provision must not be made unless:
-- src:791 | (c) the notice has been withdrawn; or
-- src:792 | (d) the first-mentioned instrument or provision is taken to have been disallowed under subsection 42(2); or
-- src:793 | (e) the motion has been withdrawn or otherwise disposed of; or
-- src:794 | (f) subsection 42(3) has applied again in relation to the first-mentioned instrument.
@ref s 47(2) (src:787-794)
GIVEN `because of subsection 42(3), the instrument is taken to have been laid before the House on a particular day` IS A BOOLEAN
      `notice of a motion to disallow has been given in that House within 15 sitting days of that House beginning on the first sitting day after that day` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice has been withdrawn` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the instrument or provision is taken to have been disallowed under subsection 42(2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the motion has been withdrawn or otherwise disposed of` IS A BOOLEAN
      `subsection 42(3) has applied again in relation to the instrument` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 47(2): the same legislative instrument or provision must not be made` MEANS
    IF NOT (`because of subsection 42(3), the instrument is taken to have been laid before the House on a particular day` AND `notice of a motion to disallow has been given in that House within 15 sitting days of that House beginning on the first sitting day after that day`) THEN NOTHING
    ELSE
        IF `the notice has been withdrawn` OR `the instrument or provision is taken to have been disallowed under subsection 42(2)` OR `the motion has been withdrawn or otherwise disposed of` OR `subsection 42(3) has applied again in relation to the instrument`
        THEN JUST FALSE
        ELSE JUST TRUE

-- src:795 | (3) A legislative instrument or a provision of a legislative instrument made in contravention of this section has no effect.
@ref s 47(3) (src:795-795)
GIVEN `the instrument or provision is made in contravention of section 47` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 47(3): the instrument or provision made in contravention has effect` MEANS
    IF `the instrument or provision is made in contravention of section 47` THEN JUST FALSE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:796 | (4) This section does not limit the operation of section 46 or 48.
@ref s 47(4) (src:796-796)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 47(4): section 47 limits the operation of section 46 or 48` MEANS JUST FALSE

-- jural: immunity of the Parliament's scrutiny of the disallowed instrument | disability of the rule-maker to remake it
-- Section 48(1): "must not be made within 6 months after the day of disallowance": the period is fixed in the text's own words, so a day outside it answers JUST FALSE;
-- where the text does not say on which day the six months end the answer is NOTHING (fork F02; the period itself is counted in lga-time.l4).
-- src:798 | (1) A legislative instrument or a provision of a legislative instrument (the later instrument or provision) that is the same in substance as a legislative instrument or a provision of a legislative instrument (the disallowed instrument or provision) that has been disallowed (or is taken to have been disallowed) under subsection 42(1) or (2) must not be made within 6 months after the day of disallowance.
-- src:799 | (2) However, the later instrument or provision may be made within that time if the relevant House of the Parliament approves, by resolution, the making of a legislative instrument or provision the same in substance as the disallowed instrument or provision.
@ref s 48(1) and (2) (src:798-799)
GIVEN `the instrument is the same in substance as an instrument disallowed (or taken to have been disallowed) under subsection 42(1) or (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day of disallowance` IS A DATE
      `the day the later instrument would be made` IS A DATE
      `the relevant House approves, by resolution, the making of an instrument the same in substance` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 48(1): the later legislative instrument or provision must not be made on that day` MEANS
    IF NOT `the instrument is the same in substance as an instrument disallowed (or taken to have been disallowed) under subsection 42(1) or (2)` THEN NOTHING
    ELSE
        CONSIDER `s 48(1): a day falls within the 6 months after the day of disallowance` `the day of disallowance` `the day the later instrument would be made`
        WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
        WHEN JUST `within` THEN
            (IF `within`
             THEN (IF `the relevant House approves, by resolution, the making of an instrument the same in substance` THEN JUST FALSE ELSE JUST TRUE)
             ELSE JUST FALSE)

@ref s 48(2) (src:799-799)
GIVEN `the day the later instrument would be made is within 6 months after the day of disallowance` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the relevant House approves, by resolution, the making of an instrument the same in substance` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 48(2): the later instrument or provision may be made within that time` MEANS
    IF `the day the later instrument would be made is within 6 months after the day of disallowance`
    THEN (IF `the relevant House approves, by resolution, the making of an instrument the same in substance` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING)
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:800 | (3) For the purposes of subsection (2), the relevant House of Parliament is the House of Parliament in which notice was given of the motion to disallow the disallowed instrument or provision.
@ref s 48(3) (src:800-800)
GIVEN `the House in which notice was given of the motion to disallow` IS A House
GIVETH A House
`s 48(3): the relevant House` MEANS `the House in which notice was given of the motion to disallow`

-- src:801 | (4) A legislative instrument or provision made in contravention of this section has no effect.
@ref s 48(4) (src:801-801)
GIVEN `the instrument or provision is made in contravention of section 48` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 48(4): the instrument or provision made in contravention has effect` MEANS
    IF `the instrument or provision is made in contravention of section 48` THEN JUST FALSE ELSE NOTHING
